<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:26:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Far-right AfD secures huge lead in key vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0dc58863cd35ee1660e42bfbd7c3f02ea826c5949477daf7b7cc549f449539</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:26:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-far-right-afd-secures-huge-lead-in-key-vote/live-78754934--631e9b0ddafb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-far-right-afd-secures-huge-lead-in-key-vote/live-78754934?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has taken a massive lead at the Saxony-Anhalt election, although it was not clear if it will be able to form government. The party's state leader said the result sends "a signal to Berlin." Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes on Lebanon kill several despite truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb3fe946d85a6e6bbc08514d527fc69d84bc89958fa24a0c667051e75691536</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:26:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-kill-several-despite-truce/a-79065011--55ceb327e7e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-kill-several-despite-truce/a-79065011?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lebanon's President Joseph Aoun has appealed to the international community to "take immediate action to stop these violations" of the ceasefire agreement between Israel and Lebanon.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff, Kushner arrive in Kiyv after Putin talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5db568c2736ae68dace514436b500366895400fb9a6fd12ae8e775b07c3f0684</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:26:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T13:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-kushner-arrive-in-kiyv-after-putin-talks/a-79054779--64e084317739.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-kushner-arrive-in-kiyv-after-putin-talks/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The two US offcials are meeting Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, with national security advisors the UK, France, and Germany reportedly also in Ukraine for talks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rahul Gandhi backs student protests in Maharashtra</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53c094f769e7cc466509d949fada0e570049059a57ebcbe8bee263cccf62a4fe</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-backs-student-protests-in-maharashtra/live-79043198--c16d7d5783ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-backs-student-protests-in-maharashtra/live-79043198?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition Rahul Gandhi has said that students are "tormented" by the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party. The Congress politician has demanded immediate action into the demands of Maharashtra student protesters. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3af635e54db9b42fb65da55928b931a2daa42682be7e8ba020eaa86ebd796734</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany plans anti-drone shield over Leipzig attack — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9411563f23efe3520750832694c85af0a2e8944277722abd2ec4a53a13b118bf</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604--572615382eed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several German cities will receive rapidly deployable units capable of defending against drone strikes on critical infrastructure, according to Bild am Sonntag newspaper.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change and food insecurity could fuel future conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed1ecd43b83ba3be9d6d61611f6219f347c9161983f5185da63028d0c8f293e9</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431--8e63f64c4115.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate change, conflict, and trade tensions are putting pressure on the global food system. New research suggests the biggest risk is not food shortages, but whether societies can peacefully adapt to change.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Flights canceled as Anak Krakatau volcano erupts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f4fc06bd30f8dd2a496b9ed43b20032f8ac5bdcd59366521e23a6f0c7b18a2</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-flights-canceled-as-anak-krakatau-volcano-erupts/a-79050871--17392aeed85d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-flights-canceled-as-anak-krakatau-volcano-erupts/a-79050871?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The spread of ash after the volcanic eruption of Anak Krakatau has impacted thousands of passengers, as flights were canceled at Jakarta's international airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why children are last to be treated in medical crises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:679ec7e61e50941d5bc4b8ce6539402e6abda01a315c5c33ba9cd84cc132d908</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107--c059b44b485e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo, children are more likely to die than adults. But it's not always due to the disease. Specific medicines for younger people are often harder to come by.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80717c624f94ae434abcfd94e8e9e0c89c1646cb50aa04bb00060d1feed3159e</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt's state election will have a nationwide impact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ca133f57184e47fabf2d9254645a10d543f35e557aea07dadc77855e4e577c1</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T01:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569--8cf3f82cd3a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The parliamentary election in the small eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt could have dramatic consequences for Germany's federal government, further raising dissatisfaction with Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys meet with Putin, leave Russia for Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90649e75d63eb2ade47d6fd0ac2aa193e0c774c8ba68f994b211fd36f9e61ad3</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-meet-with-putin-leave-russia-for-kyiv/a-79040773--6af20c7cc1f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-meet-with-putin-leave-russia-for-kyiv/a-79040773?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Moscow to try to revive talks to end the war in Ukraine. The US envoys are also scheduled to visit Kyiv on Sunday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German company successfully launches rocket to space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9316100a48bb5db26090e6d69d25e8098754eb0b7bf364e94279e5e222d49229</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717--59c961471bc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bavaria-based Isar Aerospace managed to launch its Spectrum rocket into orbit, 18 months after its first attempt. This is the first such launch from European soil.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:658c46681ac9a81c7d08c3d356dcae11a6c09532240bc033f233f33cf62439b3</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Masked anti-migrant protesters block UK's Dover terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:051b8505fb4658774d89262382c75d4df71b71d1b11c6d5998ba3f79c7d2ef97</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/masked-anti-migrant-protesters-block-uk-s-dover-terminal/a-79046929--f6606768718e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/masked-anti-migrant-protesters-block-uk-s-dover-terminal/a-79046929?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chanting "stop the boats" and wearing balaclavas, the demonstrators blocked traffic at the UK's busiest international ferry port.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's postal voting system isn't rigged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c71468692fca48f92c1c3ba17281714a8a63112aaa7cdd6aa5723377e5202a7</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438--ffb06136be22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Germany heads into three elections in September, rumors are circulating on social media claiming that postal voting is not secure — claims that have also been made about other elections. Here's why they're wrong.</summary><category term="German election" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: US hits 3 IRGC-linked oil tankers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25288e2bdd4309875f68de86af7cb3a4a86a83fba301205fd72d5fcb501f1046</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-us-hits-3-irgc-linked-oil-tankers/live-79044467--62e9bb33b870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-us-hits-3-irgc-linked-oil-tankers/live-79044467?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US military said it had destroyed three vessels linked to Iran's Revolutionary Guards. Tehran responded by threatening to increase strikes on US ships in the region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:667694ed1b15fecd6e316c50f8c846b6fb3e0e0af334f6523e4cdc6489231404</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why many Syrians feel Assad death sentence isn't enough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c0e857d022d7ec33b53b53b85a237c20b73000af4aa4c4de360146e7625837d</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915--4ab418802105.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-many-syrians-feel-assad-death-sentence-isn-t-enough/a-78985915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In July, a Syrian court sentenced former dictator Bashar Assad to death for crimes against his own people. But after 14 years of civil war, many survivors are demanding more when it comes to transitional justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands march at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5ed0ac2a752eeb42653936171a46e909629bf6351e1da9eade29d64e0854a1</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--28cda5652dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups has been held in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD organized its final campaign rally in the state capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be5d18e9f2dfde0ae59da78ddf7e9592132ad1c12e2a3575ec7dc0118e82e33e</id><updated>2026-09-06T18:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
